# wide_call_stack_unwind.tcyr — 6.6.20. A call with any number of arguments takes back exactly the
# stack it pushed, and the callee reads every one of them — direct and through `callptr`.
#
# ⛔ THE DEFECT (aarch64 ELF and arm64 Mach-O, every release through 6.6.19). ECALLCLEAN dropped a
# call's stack arguments with ONE `add sp, sp, #imm12` of (n - 6) * 16 bytes, and nothing guarded
# the immediate (the frame prologue's EPATCHFRAME already split it). From 262 arguments the carry
# landed in the LSL #12 bit:
#   262      `add sp, sp, #0, lsl #12` — sp never restored; a looped call walks off the stack (SIGSEGV)
#   263      +64 KiB where +4112 is right — sp climbs over the caller's own frame; a looped call
#            overwrites its own counter and never ends (measured: still running after 10 minutes)
#   518      the carry reaches bit 23 — an `addg` on an MTE core such as qemu's default cpu (sp
#            silently leaks), SIGILL on pi and Apple Silicon (measured on pi: exit 132)
#   519+     SIGILL everywhere, at the first call
# Silent below that: one 300-argument call "works" while nothing touches the displaced sp. Past 2048
# arguments the marshalling loads/stores (`ldr/str xN, [sp, #imm]`) carried their scaled imm12 into
# opc bit 22: each `ldr` read a slot 32 KiB too low, and the shuffle's `str` assembled as an `ldr`
# (the store vanished); from 2054 parameters the callee's `ldr x9, [x29, #imm]` did the same (at
# 2054 it read the saved fp). And from 8192 parameters the callee homed and read its parameters
# through a 16-bit `movz` of the displacement — param 8192 was written over the saved fp — the same
# truncation that made any local after a 64 KiB buffer alias a byte inside it (the frame rows). All
# now split, go through x16, or carry bits 16..31 in a `movk`. The x86 targets were never affected;
# the rows run on every host so a future regression anywhere is caught.
#
# ON cx the 261..600-argument rows run since 6.7.6, when a cx call stopped holding every argument
# in a register (arguments 248+ go in the guest stack, as SysV passes 7+; before it, 249 arguments
# gave a wrong value and 252 trapped). The 2100 / 8200 rows stay inside `#ifndef
# CYRIUS_TARGET_CX`: their thresholds are aarch64 immediates, and with them the bytecode fills
# most of cx's 512 KiB code buffer. The frame rows run
# there because cx had the same 16-bit truncation by frame size: ESUBRSP reserved a lone
# `movi r252, size` and EPATCHFRAME patched only `size & 0xFFFF` into it, so a frame of 64 KiB or
# more lowered sp by size mod 64 KiB and every callee frame landed inside the caller's buffer (a
# 66000-byte frame filled byte by byte by a callee never finished: the fill overwrote the callee's
# own counter). ESUBRSP now carries a `movhi r252` slot for bits 16..31. tests/gates/codegen/
# wide_call_stack_unwind.sh runs this file on cxvm.
#
# Each row: the value the callee computes from six parameter positions (first, the last register
# one, the first stack one, the middle, the last) against a literal, and `spp()` — the address of a
# local in a fresh callee frame, i.e. the caller's sp at the call — before and after, which must
# match. The looped rows only loop when the single call left sp balanced: on the broken compiler the
# 263 loop never terminates, and a gate must fail, not hang.
# CROSS-HOST: aarch64 is pi (ELF) and ecb (arm64 Mach-O); the generated, qemu-run twin with the
# exact thresholds is tests/gates/codegen/wide_call_stack_unwind.sh.
include "lib/syscalls.cyr"
include "lib/alloc.cyr"
include "lib/string.cyr"
include "lib/fnptr.cyr"
include "lib/assert.cyr"

# The caller's stack pointer at this call, as seen from a fresh frame.
fn spp() { var x = 1; return &x; }

